    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) or shows increasing negativity.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes by applying a 1-2 day lag correction.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is > 10% above recent 5-day average, reduce by 5-10%.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to sentiment when sentiment > 0.50 — especially in early/medium horizon.",
    "For long-term (30d) forecasts, cap upward bias at +5% above recent 15-day high to avoid overestimation.",
    "When sentiment is positive and price is trending down, reduce forecast slope to avoid premature reversal."
